<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>kjk: third-party licences</title>
<style>
body { font: 15px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 52rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; color: #222; background: #fff; }
pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1rem; font-size: 13px; }
h2 { border-top: 1px solid #ccc; padding-top: 1.5rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Third-party licences</h1>
<p>kjk is MIT (see LICENSE and NOTICE). It is built from the Rust crates
below, under the licences they carry. The MPL-2.0 crates are used unmodified;
their source is at the crates.io link beside each.</p>
<h2>Overview</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}<li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}</ul>
{{#each licenses}}
<h2 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h2>
<p>Used by:</p>
<ul>
{{#each used_by}}<li><a href="https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}/{{crate.version}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
{{/each}}</ul>
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
{{/each}}
</body>
</html>
